From 54000f0f0b650e3b67aeb1fb39baec596f3b8147 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:14:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Dreadwatch, Wallguard, Warden: list addresses on their rows,
 new lists fetched on Save

- shared/reaper_lists.h (new): every built-in Dreadwatch and Wallguard list address in one place,
  used by rc (rwarden.c, wallguard.c) and by httpd's new reaper_list_urls ej, so each page row
  shows the address it downloads before the list is ticked (forum request).
- Wallguard: Save from the page runs a sync - a list ticked for the first time, or again after its
  copy was pruned, is downloaded then instead of waiting for the nightly run. The DNS-bypass check
  also finds a DNAT inside a chain a port-53 rule jumps to (VPN Director's Exclusive DNS).
- Warden: the global IPv6 prefix of every LAN-side bridge returns before the country sets and
  feeds (a Guest Network Pro or VLAN network with its own prefix met the drops when your own
  country was blocked); the router's WAN addresses are left out.
- Encrypted DNS: AiMesh nodes are exempt from REAPER_EDNS, as from every other enforcement chain.
- Reaper_Dreadwatch.asp: the device counters list every device kept (the 100 busiest).
- 25 language packs: help text for the above (RWDN_11, RWDN_18, RWDN_111, RWDN_118, RSHD_133,
  RDWT_68).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
